      "writtenOn": "2017-07-20T19:37:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "oh, so with \n\n1000000/(8*32768) \u003d 3.81 \n\nthe approximation of usec_per_tick to 4 is indeed way too rough.\n\nI still don\u0027t think this complexity is required, as the number of ticks is integer.\n\nhow about ((usecs * 1000/3815) + 1)\n\nwill be a much simpler calculation with adequate accuracy.\n\nAlso, why are you replacing functions with macros? I think even \u0027inline\u0027 keyword is not required - the compiler inlines small static functions on its own.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "c89dda3d2c3a6f2a36f37607b9fe9d141d58b433",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3739c39f_864b8cef",
        "filename": "chip/g/hwtimer.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-20T20:59:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ignoring the details of the 64-bit division algorithm, your proposal does not lead to a simpler calculation than the calculation I commented above. usecs is on [0,0xffffffff], so multiplying by 1000 requires us to use a 64-bit intermediate type, followed by a 64-bit division that will require a call to __aeabi_uldivmod().\n\nRegarding macros vs functions (or inline functions), I think macros are more appropriate here and easier to understand, but I will change back to functions if you think it best.",
      "parentUuid": "1796c443_90079722",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "c89dda3d2c3a6f2a36f37607b9fe9d141d58b433",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
